# walk_controls · walk around the scene yourself: the thumb stick (or WASD) to walk, a drag (or the mouse) to look
# walk_controls(at, look_at, walk, run, eye) makes the scene a game (`mode "game"`) and stands the player at `at`,
# looking at `look_at` (5 m ahead if not given), walking at `walk` m/s (1.4, a person's pace), running at `run` (4),
# with their eyes `eye` metres up (1.65). Drop it where the player should start.
# kind: script
# place: walk_controls(AT)
# credit: J Production, made in Loop3D
# licence: our own work, free for every J Production project
# from: the library's Scripts shelf (2026-11-23)
# tags: controls, walk, first person, player, game, start, stick, script
to walk_controls(at: vec(0, 0, 0), look_at: nothing, walk: 1.4, run: 4, eye: 1.65)
  mode "game"
  setting "player.walk", walk
  setting "player.run", run
  setting "player.eye", eye
  move_player(at, look_at: at + vec(0, eye, -5) if look_at == nothing else look_at)
